textures are NOT reused - texPaths here point at the donor's texture ONLY as a
loud temporary placeholder until fill_queue.py renders land (art jobs filed
separately, rimflow_item_id DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1).

CUSTOM BODY SUBSTITUTION (not a framework drop, a scope call): five species used
Alpha Animals' own custom BodyDefs (AA_EyeBody, AA_SentientPlant, AA_Squid,
AA_WormWithArmorAndTusks, AA_ArmouredSlug), each with its own BodyPartDef graph
in a shared BodyParts_Animal.xml. Porting that whole graph (further BodyPartDef
chains) was cut for scope; instead each creature uses the closest EXISTING
vanilla BodyDef, confirmed by inspecting that BodyDef's own part tree (never
guessed): Eyeling and SandSquid -> Monkey (HeadAttackTool + Teeth groups
present); Needleroll/Needlepost -> QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail (same body
Cactipine/SandProwler already use, Teeth + HeadAttackTool present);
MammothWorm -> Snake (HeadAttackTool present on SnakeHead, "Mouth" group on
SnakeMouth). Every tool's linkedBodyPartsGroup below was remapped to a group
tag confirmed present on the substitute body; this changes hit-location
granularity, not stats or behaviour. Custom ToolCapacityDefs (AA_ToxicSting,
AA_ToxicBite, AA_SiegeBlunt, AA_ExtraDamageMechanoidsTusk) are likewise
substituted with the nearest vanilla capacity (Scratch/Bite/Blunt/Poke) rather
than ported with their donor DamageDef/HediffDef poison chain - a deliberate
mechanic drop, documented per species below.

wildBiomes are omitted throughout - biome-table rewiring is a later step the
parent runs (WORLD_REMAKE_FINAL_STEP_1 / this item's own sequencing section).
